@prefix : <http://example.org/trust-domain#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix gist: <https://w3id.org/semanticarts/ns/ontology/gist/> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@base <http://example.org/trust-domain#> .

<http://example.org/trust-domain> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Trust Domain Ontology"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """Canonical ontology for private & foreign irrevocable non-grantor trust domains, modeling authority, instruments, and operational boundaries.

This ontology treats tax code sections not as 'tax rules' but as recognized instruments, authority boundaries, evidence schemas, and control-plane components.

CRITICAL ARCHITECTURE:
- IRC §§671-679: The GATEWAY - creates separation between grantor and trust (control-of-income boundary)
- IRC §§641-685: The OPERATING SYSTEM - enables trust as autonomous accounting system (DNI, distributions, character flow-through)
- IRC §7701: The JURISDICTION - assigns which sovereign's rules apply (court + control tests)
- IRC §162/§212/§67(e): The EXPENSE INSTRUMENTS - operational spending power for trusts
- EIN: System identifier (MAC address, not protocol) - NOT an instrument

THE KEYSTONE CONSTRAINT:
Private enablement is permissible when and only when it is BOTH:
  1. Incidental to purpose-driven execution (not the primary purpose), AND
  2. Inseparable from purpose-driven execution (necessarily coupled with mission advancement)

This constraint is the fundamental boundary between legitimate operations and private inurement.
All compensation, benefits, and private enablement must satisfy both tests to be permissible.

THE AUTHORITY CASCADE (PROOF OF LEGITIMACY):
Mission → Purpose Domains → Authorized Activities → Operators in Role → Expense Domains → Actual Spend

Every dollar spent MUST trace back through this cascade to mission/purpose. This traceable chain PROVES
keystone constraint satisfaction. If spend cannot trace back to purpose through authorized activity and
required operator, it fails the keystone constraint and constitutes private inurement.

The cascade enforces:
- Mission legitimizes Authority (purpose → power)
- Purpose authorizes Activities (what trust may do)
- Activities require Operators (who executes)
- Operators necessitate Expense Domains (enablement categories)
- Expense Domains manifest as Actual Spend (dollars out)
- Actual Spend traces back to Purpose (closes the loop)

TEMPORAL DIMENSION:
- All expenditures occur during temporal periods (fiscal years, quarters, months)
- DNI computed annually per fiscal year
- Qualifying distributions tracked against minimum distribution requirements (IRC §4942)
- Enables time-series queries and fiscal year compliance tracking

GRANTMAKING (DISTINCT FROM OPERATIONS):
- GrantmakingActivity as separate authorized activity class
- Grants to public charities count as qualifying distributions
- Non-exempt grantees require expenditure responsibility
- Program-Related Investments (PRIs) as grants for charitable purpose

IRC §§4941-4945 SAFEGUARDS (FULLY AXIOMATIZED):
- §4941: Self-dealing prohibition - transactions with disqualified persons
- §4942: Minimum distribution requirements - qualifying distributions vs. minimum
- §4943: Excess business holdings - ownership percentage limits
- §4944: Jeopardizing investments - investments endangering mission
- §4945: Taxable expenditures - lobbying, political, grants without responsibility

All safeguards are disjoint classes with prohibited behaviors triggering AuthorityCollapse.

Non-grantor and foreign trusts acquire operational instruments once control, jurisdiction, and fiduciary authority are cleanly separated under the doctrinal stack."""@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "4.0" .

#################################################################
#    Object Properties
#################################################################

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#exercisesAuthority
:exercisesAuthority rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustEntity ;
    rdfs:range :Authority ;
    rdfs:label "exercises authority"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Relates a trust entity to the authority it exercises"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#advancesPurpose
:advancesPurpose rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :OperationalActivity ;
    rdfs:range :Purpose ;
    rdfs:label "advances purpose"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links an operational activity to the purpose it advances"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#implementedBy
:implementedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Purpose ;
    rdfs:range :Instrument ;
    rdfs:label "implemented by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Relates a purpose to the instruments that implement it"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#substantiatedBy
:substantiatedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Instrument ;
    rdfs:range :Evidence ;
    rdfs:label "substantiated by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links an instrument to the evidence that substantiates it"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#governedBy
:governedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Instrument ;
    rdfs:range :DoctrinalSource ;
    rdfs:label "governed by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Indicates which doctrinal source governs an instrument"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasBeneficiary
:hasBeneficiary rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustStructure ;
    rdfs:range :Beneficiary ;
    rdfs:label "has beneficiary"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasTrustee
:hasTrustee rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustStructure ;
    rdfs:range :Trustee ;
    rdfs:label "has trustee"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasProtector
:hasProtector rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustStructure ;
    rdfs:range :Protector ;
    rdfs:label "has protector"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#employs
:employs rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustEntity ;
    rdfs:range :HumanCapability ;
    rdfs:label "employs"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Relates trust entity to human capabilities it employs"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#controls
:controls rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustEntity ;
    rdfs:range :Asset ;
    rdfs:label "controls"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Indicates asset control relationship"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#incurs
:incurs rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustEntity ;
    rdfs:range :Expenditure ;
    rdfs:label "incurs"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Relates entity to expenditures it incurs"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#withinBoundary
:withinBoundary rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :OperationalActivity ;
    rdfs:range :OperatingBoundary ;
    rdfs:label "within boundary"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Indicates activity is within operational boundary"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#requiresEvidence
:requiresEvidence rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Instrument ;
    rdfs:range :EvidenceDiscipline ;
    rdfs:label "requires evidence"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#preventsMisuse
:preventsMisuse rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :SafeguardMechanism ;
    rdfs:range :AuthorityCollapse ;
    rdfs:label "prevents misuse"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#retainsControlPower
:retainsControlPower rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Grantor ;
    rdfs:range :ControlPower ;
    rdfs:label "retains control power"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Grantor retains enumerated control power under IRC §§671-679"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#lacksRetainedControl
:lacksRetainedControl rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :NonGrantorTrustSystem ;
    rdfs:range :ControlPower ;
    rdfs:label "lacks retained control"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Trust lacks enumerated control powers, crossing the non-grantor boundary"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#makesDistribution
:makesDistribution rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :NonGrantorTrustSystem ;
    rdfs:range :Distribution ;
    rdfs:label "makes distribution"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Trust distributes income or corpus to beneficiaries"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#passesJurisdictionalTest
:passesJurisdictionalTest rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustStructure ;
    rdfs:range :JurisdictionalTest ;
    rdfs:label "passes jurisdictional test"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Trust satisfies court or control test for jurisdictional classification"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasSystemIdentifier
:hasSystemIdentifier rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustEntity ;
    rdfs:range :SystemIdentifier ;
    rdfs:label "has system identifier"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Trust has system identifier (EIN) - not an instrument, but required for interaction"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#computesDNI
:computesDNI rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :NonGrantorTrustSystem ;
    rdfs:range :DistributableNetIncome ;
    rdfs:label "computes DNI"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Trust computes Distributable Net Income per IRC §§641-685"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#flowsCharacterThrough
:flowsCharacterThrough rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Distribution ;
    rdfs:range :CharacterFlowThrough ;
    rdfs:label "flows character through"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Distribution carries income character to beneficiary"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#requiresFiling
:requiresFiling rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :NonGrantorTrustSystem ;
    rdfs:range :FiduciaryReturn ;
    rdfs:label "requires filing"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Trust must file fiduciary tax return (Form 1041)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasPurpose
:hasPurpose rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustEntity ;
    rdfs:range :Purpose ;
    rdfs:label "has purpose"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Trust entity has stated purpose that legitimizes its authority"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasSubPurpose
:hasSubPurpose rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Purpose ;
    rdfs:range :Purpose ;
    rdfs:label "has sub-purpose"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Purpose composed of multiple sub-purposes or mission areas"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#isIncidentalTo
:isIncidentalTo rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :PrivateEnablement ;
    rdfs:range :Purpose ;
    rdfs:label "is incidental to"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Private enablement is incidental to purpose-driven execution"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#isInseparableFrom
:isInseparableFrom rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :PrivateEnablement ;
    rdfs:range :OperationalActivity ;
    rdfs:label "is inseparable from"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Private enablement is inseparable from operational execution"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#enablesPrivately
:enablesPrivately rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Instrument ;
    rdfs:range :PrivateEnablement ;
    rdfs:label "enables privately"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Instrument provides private enablement (compensation, benefits, etc.)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#satisfiesKeystoneConstraint
:satisfiesKeystoneConstraint rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :PrivateEnablement ;
    rdfs:range :KeystoneConstraint ;
    rdfs:label "satisfies keystone constraint"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Private enablement satisfies the keystone constraint: incidental to AND inseparable from purpose-driven execution"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#violatesKeystoneConstraint
:violatesKeystoneConstraint rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :PrivateEnablement ;
    rdfs:range :KeystoneConstraint ;
    rdfs:label "violates keystone constraint"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Private enablement violates keystone constraint - not incidental or separable from purpose"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasMarketBenchmark
:hasMarketBenchmark rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf gist:hasMagnitude ;
    rdfs:domain :PrivateEnablement ;
    rdfs:range gist:Magnitude ;
    rdfs:label "has market benchmark"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The market-rate amount for comparable services, as a gist:Magnitude in USD with hasPaymentPeriod and dcterms:source. Spend above it is the separable excess the keystone check fails. (Proposed 2026-11-19.)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasPaymentPeriod
:hasPaymentPeriod rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf gist:isCategorizedBy ;
    rdfs:range :PaymentPeriod ;
    rdfs:label "has payment period"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "How often an amount recurs (per month, per year, one time), so the keystone check can compare a payment with its benchmark. (Proposed 2026-11-19.)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#buildsCapability
:buildsCapability rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :AuthorizedActivity ;
    rdfs:range :LongTermCapability ;
    rdfs:label "builds capability"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Links a program (authorized activity) to the lasting capability it builds. This is the second half of the mission: health, education, innovation and opportunity are the means; long-term human and systemic capability is the end. (Proposed 2026-11-20.)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#capabilityTest
:capabilityTest rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :LongTermCapability ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "capability test"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The evidence that would show the capability lasted, stated before the money is spent. (Proposed 2026-11-20.)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#deployedIn
:deployedIn rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Asset ;
    rdfs:range :AuthorizedActivity ;
    rdfs:label "deployed in"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The asset-to-program link: the program an asset is held for. No asset sits outside a program. (Proposed 2026-11-20.)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#grantedUnder
:grantedUnder rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Grant ;
    rdfs:range :GrantmakingActivity ;
    rdfs:label "granted under"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The grantmaking program a grant is made under, so a grant traces back through the cascade like any other spend. (Proposed 2026-11-20.)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#ProgramParticipant
:ProgramParticipant rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf gist:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Program participant"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A member of the public a program serves. (Proposed 2026-11-20.)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#participatesIn
:participatesIn rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ProgramParticipant ;
    rdfs:range :AuthorizedActivity ;
    rdfs:label "participates in"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#ParticipantRecord
:ParticipantRecord rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf gist:Content ;
    rdfs:label "Participant record"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A record a participant keeps about themselves through a program, such as their own health graph. It belongs to the participant, not the foundation: it is never a foundation asset, and it leaves the participant's hands only with their own revocable consent. (Proposed 2026-11-20.)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#ownedBy
:ownedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ParticipantRecord ;
    rdfs:range :ProgramParticipant ;
    rdfs:label "owned by"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#heldUnder
:heldUnder rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ParticipantRecord ;
    rdfs:range :AuthorizedActivity ;
    rdfs:label "held under"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The program that gives the participant the tools to keep the record."@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#sharedWith
:sharedWith rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ParticipantRecord ;
    rdfs:label "shared with"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Anyone outside the participant's own device who receives the record or part of it."@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#ConsentRecord
:ConsentRecord rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Consent record"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "One consent, given by the record's owner, to one named recipient for one scope, always revocable. Sharing is off by default. (Proposed 2026-11-20.)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasConsent
:hasConsent rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ParticipantRecord ;
    rdfs:range :ConsentRecord ;
    rdfs:label "has consent"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#grantedBy
:grantedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ConsentRecord ;
    rdfs:range :ProgramParticipant ;
    rdfs:label "granted by"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#consentFor
:consentFor rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ConsentRecord ;
    rdfs:label "consent for"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The named recipient the consent covers."@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#consentScope
:consentScope rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ConsentRecord ;
    rdfs:range :ConsentScope ;
    rdfs:label "consent scope"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#consentRevocable
:consentRevocable rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ConsentRecord ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "consent revocable"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Must be true: the owner can withdraw it at any time."@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#ConsentScope
:ConsentScope rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf gist:Category ;
    rdfs:label "Consent scope"@en .
:LocalOnly rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConsentScope ;
    rdfs:label "Local only (default: nothing leaves the owner's device)"@en .
:SharedWithNamedRecipient rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConsentScope ;
    rdfs:label "Shared with one named recipient the owner chose"@en .
:DeidentifiedResearch rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :ConsentScope ;
    rdfs:label "De-identified research contribution"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#benefitsPerson
:benefitsPerson rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range gist:Person ;
    rdfs:label "benefits person"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A specific person a payment or grant benefits. The self-dealing check fails any that benefits a disqualified person other than as pay for services, which the keystone check tests for reasonableness. (Proposed 2026-11-20.)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#PaymentPeriod
:PaymentPeriod rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf gist:Category ;
    rdfs:label "Payment period"@en .
:PerMonth rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PaymentPeriod ; rdfs:label "Per month"@en .
:PerYear rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PaymentPeriod ; rdfs:label "Per year"@en .
:OneTime rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual , :PaymentPeriod ; rdfs:label "One time"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#LongTermCapability
:LongTermCapability rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :Purpose ;
    rdfs:label "Long-term capability"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A lasting human or systemic capability a program builds: the end the mission names after 'in furtherance of'."@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#legitimizes
:legitimizes rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Purpose ;
    rdfs:range :Authority ;
    rdfs:label "legitimizes"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Mission/Purpose legitimizes the exercise of Authority"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#authorizes
:authorizes rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Purpose ;
    rdfs:range :AuthorizedActivity ;
    rdfs:label "authorizes"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Purpose domain authorizes specific operational activities"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#requires
:requires rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :AuthorizedActivity ;
    rdfs:range :OperatorInRole ;
    rdfs:label "requires"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Authorized activity requires operators in specific roles"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#necessitates
:necessitates rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :OperatorInRole ;
    rdfs:range :ExpenseDomain ;
    rdfs:label "necessitates"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Operator in role necessitates expense domains (enablement)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#manifestsAs
:manifestsAs rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ExpenseDomain ;
    rdfs:range :ActualSpend ;
    rdfs:label "manifests as"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Expense domain manifests as actual spend/expenditure"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#tracesBackTo
:tracesBackTo rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ActualSpend ;
    rdfs:range :Purpose ;
    rdfs:label "traces back to"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Actual spend traces back through the authority cascade to mission/purpose"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#performedBy
:performedBy rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :AuthorizedActivity ;
    rdfs:range :OperatorInRole ;
    rdfs:label "performed by"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Authorized activity is performed by operator in role"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#sustains
:sustains rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ExpenseDomain ;
    rdfs:range :OperatorInRole ;
    rdfs:label "sustains"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Expense domain sustains the operator's capability to perform"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#servesActivity
:servesActivity rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :OperatorInRole ;
    rdfs:range :AuthorizedActivity ;
    rdfs:label "serves activity"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Operator in role serves the authorized activity"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#occursDuring
:occursDuring rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ActualSpend ;
    rdfs:range :TemporalPeriod ;
    rdfs:label "occurs during"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Expenditure occurs during temporal period (fiscal year, quarter, etc.)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#computedFor
:computedFor rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :DistributableNetIncome ;
    rdfs:range :FiscalYear ;
    rdfs:label "computed for"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "DNI computed for specific fiscal year"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasTemporalExtent
:hasTemporalExtent rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :OperationalActivity ;
    rdfs:range :TemporalPeriod ;
    rdfs:label "has temporal extent"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Activity spans temporal period"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#makesGrant
:makesGrant rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustEntity ;
    rdfs:range :Grant ;
    rdfs:label "makes grant"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Trust entity makes charitable grant"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#receivesGrant
:receivesGrant rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Grantee ;
    rdfs:range :Grant ;
    rdfs:label "receives grant"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Grantee receives grant from trust"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#satisfiesQualifyingDistribution
:satisfiesQualifyingDistribution rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Grant ;
    rdfs:range :QualifyingDistribution ;
    rdfs:label "satisfies qualifying distribution"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Grant counts toward qualifying distribution requirement (IRC §4942)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#involvesDisqualifiedPerson
:involvesDisqualifiedPerson rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Transaction ;
    rdfs:range :DisqualifiedPerson ;
    rdfs:label "involves disqualified person"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Transaction involves disqualified person (triggers IRC §4941 review)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#constitutesExcessBenefit
:constitutesExcessBenefit rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Transaction ;
    rdfs:range :ExcessBenefit ;
    rdfs:label "constitutes excess benefit"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Transaction provides excess benefit to disqualified person"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#jeopardizesMission
:jeopardizesMission rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Investment ;
    rdfs:range :Purpose ;
    rdfs:label "jeopardizes mission"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Investment jeopardizes ability to carry out mission (IRC §4944 violation)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#constitutesExcessHolding
:constitutesExcessHolding rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Investment ;
    rdfs:range :ExcessBusinessHolding ;
    rdfs:label "constitutes excess holding"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Investment constitutes excess business holding (IRC §4943 violation)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#isTaxableExpenditure
:isTaxableExpenditure rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Expenditure ;
    rdfs:range :TaxableExpenditure ;
    rdfs:label "is taxable expenditure"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Expenditure is taxable expenditure under IRC §4945"@en .

#################################################################
#    Data Properties
#################################################################

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#isRevocable
:isRevocable rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustStructure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "is revocable"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#isGrantorTrust
:isGrantorTrust rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustStructure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "is grantor trust"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#isForeign
:isForeign rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustStructure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "is foreign"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasBusinessPurpose
:hasBusinessPurpose rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :OperationalActivity ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "has business purpose"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#isOrdinaryAndNecessary
:isOrdinaryAndNecessary rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Expenditure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "is ordinary and necessary"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#isCapitalExpense
:isCapitalExpense rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Expenditure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "is capital expense"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasUsefulLife
:hasUsefulLife rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Asset ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:label "has useful life"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Useful life in years for depreciation purposes"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#establishedDate
:establishedDate rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustStructure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date ;
    rdfs:label "established date"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#jurisdiction
:jurisdiction rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustStructure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "jurisdiction"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#isDomestic
:isDomestic rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustStructure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "is domestic"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Trust satisfies domestic trust tests under IRC §7701(a)(30)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasEIN
:hasEIN rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustEntity ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "has EIN"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Employer Identification Number - system identifier, not instrument"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#dniAmount
:dniAmount rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :DistributableNetIncome ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:label "DNI amount"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Distributable Net Income amount for tax year"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasCourtJurisdiction
:hasCourtJurisdiction rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustStructure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "has court jurisdiction"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Court jurisdiction controlling trust administration"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasControlLocation
:hasControlLocation rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :TrustStructure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "has control location"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Location where substantial trust decisions are made"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#hasMissionStatement
:hasMissionStatement rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Purpose ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "has mission statement"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "The formal mission statement articulating the purpose"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#purposeDescription
:purposeDescription rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Purpose ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "purpose description"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Detailed description of the purpose and how it will be advanced"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#fiscalYearStart
:fiscalYearStart rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :FiscalYear ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date ;
    rdfs:label "fiscal year start"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Start date of fiscal year"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#fiscalYearEnd
:fiscalYearEnd rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :FiscalYear ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date ;
    rdfs:label "fiscal year end"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "End date of fiscal year"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#yearNumber
:yearNumber rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :FiscalYear ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:label "year number"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Calendar year number (e.g., 2024)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#expenditureDate
:expenditureDate rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :ActualSpend ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date ;
    rdfs:label "expenditure date"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Date expenditure was made"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#grantAmount
:grantAmount rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :Grant ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:label "grant amount"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Amount of charitable grant"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#minimumDistributionRequired
:minimumDistributionRequired rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :FiscalYear ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:label "minimum distribution required"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Minimum qualifying distribution required for fiscal year (IRC §4942)"@en .

###  http://example.org/trust-domain#qualifyingDistributionsMade
:qualifyingDistributionsMade rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain :FiscalYear ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:label "qualifying distributions made"@en ;
